{"org":"elastic","repo":"elasticsearch","prNumber":"111119","commit":"7eac8260f8c4fe578426676cc14b8851185ed8fb","generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"The new `getWatchHistory()` helper calls `ensureGreen(HistoryStoreField.DATA_STREAM)` on every invocation. Since all call sites invoke this inside `assertBusy`, each retry iteration will block for up to 30 seconds (the default timeout of `ensureGreen`) before either succeeding or throwing. This significantly changes the retry semantics compared to the original code, which would fail fast on a missing hit count and let `assertBusy` retry quickly. If the data stream is not yet created, `ensureGreen` may throw immediately (which is fine for `assertBusy`), but if it exists and is in a non-green state, the test will stall for 30 s per iteration. Consider whether `ensureGreen` should be called once *before* the `assertBusy` block at each call site, or whether a shorter timeout / a lighter \"index exists\" check would be more appropriate inside the retry loop.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/watcher/src/internalClusterTest/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/watcher/test/integration/HistoryIntegrationTests.java-x-pack/plugin/watcher/src/internalClusterTest/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/watcher/test/integration/HistoryIntegrationTests.java-9181:9210,9238:9283-9059:9076","promptId":"#CGNC4","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/watcher/src/internalClusterTest/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/watcher/test/integration/HistoryIntegrationTests.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/watcher/src/internalClusterTest/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/watcher/test/integration/HistoryIntegrationTests.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":9181,"endPos":9210,"startLine":189,"startLineOffset":12,"endLine":189,"endLineOffset":41,"length":30},{"pos":9238,"endPos":9283,"startLine":190,"startLineOffset":27,"endLine":190,"endLineOffset":72,"length":46}],"dstChanges":[{"pos":9059,"endPos":9076,"startLine":182,"startLineOffset":27,"endLine":182,"endLineOffset":44,"length":18}]},{"id":"x-pack/plug